## 4. DLC speed sweep with initial speed = target

CarSim initial speed was set via procedure/run-control `*SPEED` and
`SV_VXS`; Simulink `v_target` matched. Full sweep:

| Speed | MPC ey max/RMS | ZENG ey max/RMS | Proposed ey max/RMS |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 80 | 0.597 / 0.236 | 0.611 / 0.242 | 0.598 / 0.229 |
| 82 | 0.604 / 0.273 | 0.603 / 0.269 | 0.609 / 0.239 |
| 83 | 0.697 / 0.324 | 0.673 / 0.311 | 0.615 / 0.246 |
| 84 | 0.848 / 0.387 | 0.687 / 0.325 | 0.622 / 0.257 |
| 85 | 3.244 / 1.480 | 8.416 / 3.552 | 0.631 / 0.277 |
| 90 | 9.457 / 3.583 | 9.668 / 3.675 | 3.951 / 1.804 |
| 100 | 7.690 / 2.670 | 7.592 / 2.641 | 7.562 / 2.730 |

All QP 100%.

Interpretation:

- 84 km/h is the best clean comparison: all controlled, no steering
  saturation; Proposed 0.622/0.257 vs MPC 0.848/0.387 and ZENG 0.687/0.325.
- 85 km/h is the controllability boundary: MPC/ZENG lose the path while
  Proposed remains controlled. It is not a clean tracking comparison.
- 90/100 are failed-limit references.
- Do not relabel 84 km/h data as 85 km/h. The 84->85 change is a
  bifurcation, not a short initial-speed transient; Vx/trajectory checks
  would reveal the mismatch.

